course: dictionary
lesson: 4810
title: Humus: the rich part of soil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Soil is not just dirt. It is a mix of broken rock, water, air and living things, and one special part of it is humus. Humus is the dark, rich part of soil, made from dead leaves, plants and animals that have rotted down.
explain: Humus is made slowly by decomposers, tiny living things that break dead matter down bit by bit. «A compost heap turns kitchen and garden waste into humus with the help of decomposers.» So a compost heap works like a humus factory.
explain: Humus is good for plants because it feeds them. Soil that is «rich in humus» is dark, crumbly and good for growing things. Humus also helps soil hold water, so plants do not dry out as quickly.
fact: Humus is the dark, rich part of soil.
fact: Humus is made from dead and rotting leaves, plants and animals.
fact: Humus feeds plants and helps them grow.
fact: Decomposers, such as worms and tiny living things, help make humus.
fact: «Loam» is a mix of sand, silt, clay and humus, and is good for most crops.
exercise: «Soil is made of broken rock, humus, water, air and living things.» What is humus? | A loud kind of rock | A plant that grows on top of soil | *A dark, rich part of soil made from dead and rotting things | The air trapped in soil
exercise: «A compost heap turns kitchen and garden waste into humus with the help of what?» | *Decomposers | Lorries | Sunshine alone | Snow
exercise: Which soil is «a mix of sand, silt, clay and humus» and is good for most plants? | Sandy soil | Solid rock | Clay soil | *Loam
test: Why does humus help soil? | It stops air getting into soil | It turns soil into solid rock | It is made only from fresh green leaves | *It feeds plants and helps soil hold water
test: Sandy soil drains water fast. What does clay soil do? | *It holds water and can become sticky and waterlogged | It turns into humus at once | It has no water at all | It drains even faster
exam: Why do decomposers matter in a garden? | *They break dead matter down into humus that feeds plants | They stop plants getting water | They make the garden dry and hard | They turn soil into sand
